e the dump file name and location directly indicate LSASS process memory was targeted, not SAM, cached credentials, or LSA secrets.","evidence":[{"event_id":"E036","field":"CommandLine","quote":"\"C:\\windows\\system32\\taskmgr.exe\" /4","ok":true},{"event_id":"E036","field":"IntegrityLevel","quote":"High","ok":true},{"event_id":"E050","field":"TargetFilename","quote":"C:\\Users\\pgustavo\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\lsass.DMP","ok":true}],"attempts":1},{"technique_id":"T1546.008","name":"Accessibility Features","parent":"Event Triggered Execution","tactics":["Privilege Escalation","Persistence"],"behavior":"AtBroker.exe launched sethc.exe (Sticky Keys) with SYSTEM privileges and full access rights, a classic accessibility feature abuse for privilege escalation.","slot":1,"reasoning":"AtBroker.exe launched sethc.exe (Sticky Keys) with SYSTEM privileges, demonstrating abuse of an accessibility feature for privilege escalation. This is the classic accessibility feature hijacking technique where the accessibility binary itself is executed with elevated privileges to gain code execution as SYSTEM.","evidence":[{"event_id":"E018","field":"ParentImage","quote":"C:\\Windows\\System32\\AtBroker.exe","ok":true},{"event_id":"E018","field":"Image","quote":"C:\\Windows\\System32\\sethc.exe","ok":true},{"event_id":"E018","field":"User","quote":"NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM","ok":true}],"attempts":1},{"technique_id":"T1021.001","name":"Remote Desktop Protocol","parent":"Remote Services","tactics":["Lateral Movement"],"behavior":"User pgustavo established an RDP session and initiated Task Manager with elevation parameters, leading to privilege escalation chain.","slot":2,"reasoning":"The evidence shows pgustavo establishing an RDP session (indicated by the SESSIONNAME registry value set to \"RDP-Tcp#5\" and the logon with explicit credentials to localhost), followed by process execution within that session. This is RDP-based remote access using valid credentials, not session hijacking or privil